<title>CANADA: Canada's Prairies to see scattered snow, showers.</title>
<headline>Canada's Prairies to see scattered snow, showers.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Prairies on Monday were forecast to see scattered snow flurries and cool temperatures, Environment Canada said.</p>
<p>Alberta should see highs between +2 to +10 Celsius with scattered snow flurries in the central region.</p>
<p>Saskatchewan should see highs of -6 to +8 Celsius with showers or wet snow in the south.</p>
<p>Manitoba should see highs of -2 to +5 Celsius with scattered snow flurries along the U.S. border.</p>
<p>((--Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548))</p>
